  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Prefill (2.5-10.3x) and decode (2.1-6.1x) speedups are measured independently per phase against different baseline maxima and cannot be multiplied into end-to-end request speedup; request-level speedup depends on prompt/output token ratio, PCIe generation, CPU vector units, and expert granularity.",
    "PDScope does not support concurrent distributed prefill/decode overlap (§6) because prefill already saturates CPU and PCIe under single-node memory constraints; multi-batch support uses phase-consolidated batching (chunk=256) and saturates by bs=16 on A100.",
    "Offline profiling requires <30 min per model on A100 using 128 ShareGPT traces and assumes sufficient host DRAM/pinned-memory headroom (512 GB DRAM constrained dual-copy baselines on 291B DeepSeek-V4-Flash).",
    "Evaluation covers system throughput, latency traces, and Top-6 routing hit rate rather than perplexity/downstream task quality (exact BF16/INT8 weights preserved by true-gate layer recompilation), and omits speculative decoding or quantized KV-cache hybrids.",
    "v1 primary source notes: footnote 1 cites anonymized GitHub placeholder nezha-Anonymous/PDScope (not publicly verified), pages 5 and 11 contain two unresolved 'Appendix §??' references (pointing to §8.7 and §8.3), and Step 3 / Eq. (6) print '|f|' where ceiling ceil(f) is semantically intended."
